:: R6-NPC-SponsorDetail [release6]
The LunaLocks sales rep, a woman named Dana, follows up via email with a phone call. She's friendly, professional, mid thirties energy, the kind of person who says let's unpack that unironically but somehow makes it work.

//"Ethan, we're really excited about this partnership. Your clip resonated with our core audience in a way we rarely see with first time creators. The authenticity was the thing. You weren't doing a bit. Or if you were, it didn't read that way."//

//"It was a punishment bet."//

//"Sure. But the way you wore it, you owned it. Our analytics showed that the sentiment around your clip was 92% positive. That's almost unheard of for crossdressing content. Usually there's a significant troll contingent. Yours was almost entirely supportive."//

She walks me through the deal. Two streams minimum per month. Two hundred dollars per stream. They provide three wigs of my choice from their catalog, refreshed quarterly. I wear one on stream, tag them in the VOD description and one social media post per stream. Standard influencer contract.

//"The only stipulation is the feminine presentation. We're a cosplay wig brand. Our audience is primarily women and nonbinary individuals who use wigs for creative expression. You resonate with that demo. EthX doesn't."//

//"Right."//

//"I want to be transparent about something, Ethan. We've seen creators take deals like this and burn out because they felt trapped in a persona. That's not what we want. If at any point you need to modify the terms, we talk. No penalties for the first three months. Think of it as a trial."//

She's being kind. The contract is fair. The money is real. The wigs will be better than anything I can afford, and all I have to do is be someone I was for one night. Someone who might already be more real than the person I've been for twenty four years.

//"Can I have the weekend to think?"//

//"Absolutely. Take your time."//

